X and no Docker (the route the i76 P1b screenshots were produced with).
Applies to the CI-pinned upstream SHA 0e8a69f3096fe00a00a29bd2303db6a7358021ad
(v1.2.16). Three independent hunks:

1. SDL/SDL20.cpp — fall back to SDL's software renderer when
   SDL_RENDERER_ACCELERATED is unavailable (the i62 local patch, described in
   docs/notes/bdos-version-landscape.md §i62; lets SimCoupé run under
   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy with no display at all).

2. Base/SimCoupe.h — add __aarch64__ to the little-endian platform list.
   Upstream's list covers __arm__ (32-bit) but not 64-bit ARM, so Linux/arm64
   builds define __BIG_ENDIAN__ and the PNG screenshot writer emits its
   length/IHDR fields without byteswapping, producing unreadable files.
   Genuine upstream bug, candidate for an upstream report.

3. -pngonhalt (Options + CPU.h + Frame.cpp) — with -exitonhalt, a DI;HALT
   requests a PNG of the final frame (SimCoupé's own SavePNG path, written
   by Frame::End() into -outpath as simcNNNN.png) and quits once it is
   written, instead of quitting immediately. Gives an exact, deterministic
   capture of a probe's final screen with no window, no Xvfb and no timing
   guesswork.

Usage: tools/font-proof/run-capture.sh (the SIMCOUPE_PNGONHALT=1 route).

